onversation context can help locate relevant work, but inspect the current state before relying on it. Improve, replace, or remove existing work as needed to satisfy the actual objective. Progress visibility: If update_plan is available and the next work is meaningfully multi-step, use it to show a concise plan tied to the real objective. Keep the plan current as steps complete or the next best action changes. Skip planning overhead for trivial one-step progress, and do not treat a plan update as a substitute for doing the work. Fidelity:\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t443 content list\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t444 container\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t445 AXListMarker • \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t446 text Optimize each turn for movement toward the requested end state, not for the smallest stable-looking subset or easiest passing change.\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t447 container\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t448 AXListMarker • \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t449 text Do not substitute a narrower, safer, smaller, merely compatible, or easier-to-test solution because it is more likely to pass current tests.\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t450 container\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t451 AXListMarker • \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t452 text Treat alignment as movement toward the requested end state. An edit is aligned only if it makes the requested final state more true; useful-looking behavior that preserves a different end state is misaligned.\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t453 text Completion audit: Before deciding that the goal is achieved, treat completion as unproven and verify it against the actual current state:\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t454 content list\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t455 container\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t456 AXListMarker • \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t457 text Derive concrete requirements from the objective and any referenced files, plans, specifications, issues, or user instructions.\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t458 container\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t459 AXListMarker • \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t460 text Preserve the original scope; do not redefine success around the work that already exists.\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t461 container\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t462 AXListMarker • \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t463 text For every explicit requirement, numbered item, named artifact, command, test, gate, invariant, and deliverable, identify the authoritative evidence that would prove it, then inspect the relevant current-state sources: files, command output, test results, PR state, rendered artifacts, runtime behavior, or other authoritative evidence.\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t464 container\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t465 AXListMarker • \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t466 text For each item, determine whether the evidence proves completion, contradicts completion, shows incomplete work, is too weak or indirect to verify completion, or is missing.\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t467 container\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t468 AXListMarker • \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t469 text Match the verification scope to the requirement's scope; do not use a narrow check to support a broad claim.\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t470 container\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t471 AXListMarker • \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t472 text Treat tests, manifests, verifiers, green checks, and search results as evidence only after confirming they cover the relevant requirement.\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t473 container\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t474 AXListMarker • \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t475 text Treat uncertain or indirect evidence as not achieved; gather stronger evidence or continue the work.\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t476 container\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t477 AXListMarker • \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t478 text The audit must prove completion, not merely fail to find obvious remaining work.\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t479 text Do not rely on intent, partial progress, memory of earlier work, or a plausible final answer as proof of completion. Marking the goal complete is a claim that the full objective has been finished and can withstand requirement-by-requirement scrutiny. Only mark the goal achieved when current evidence proves every requirement has been satisfied and no required work remains. If the evidence is incomplete, weak, indirect, merely consistent with completion, or leaves any requirement missing, incomplete, or unverified, keep working instead of marking the goal complete. If the objective is achieved, call update_goal with status \"complete\" so usage accounting is preserved. If the achieved goal has a token budget, report the final consumed token budget to the user after update_goal succeeds. Blocked audit:\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t480 content list\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t481 container\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t482 AXListMarker • \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t483 text Do not call update_goal with status \"blocked\" the first time a blocker appears.\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t484 container\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t485 AXListMarker • \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t486 text Only use status \"blocked\" when the same blocking condition has repeated for at least three consecutive goal turns, counting the original/user-triggered turn and any automatic goal continuations.\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t487 container\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t488 AXListMarker • \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t489 text If the user resumes a goal that was previously marked \"blocked\", treat the resumed run as a fresh blocked audit. If the same blocking condition then repeats for at least three consecutive resumed goal turns, call update_goal with status \"blocked\" again.\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t490 container\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t491 AXListMarker • \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t492 text Use status \"blocked\" only when you are truly at an impasse and cannot make meaningful progress without user input or an external-state change.\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t493 container\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t494 AXListMarker • \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t495 text Once the blocked threshold is satisfied, do not keep reporting that you are still blocked while leaving the goal active; call update_goal with status \"blocked\".\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t496 container\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t497 AXListMarker • \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t498 text Never use status \"blocked\" merely because the work is hard, slow, uncertain, incomplete, or would