rrent file, accessible determinate progress, and workspace-refresh phase while disabling duplicate submission; successful files enter reviewed assembly immediately and the final best-effort report remains itemized. Manual assembly remains as the controlled fallback for deliberate 2–100-file composition, rejecting missing documents, unsafe relative paths, duplicate selection ids, case-insensitive duplicate archive paths, and per-file/aggregate size overflow while preserving an existing manifest or generating compatible IMS aliases from paths, original XML metadata, and Verona JSON-LD module identity/version metadata\n+- loose source-package intake resolves unique original `Booklet` or `SysCheck` → `Unit` → Verona player, `DefinitionRef`, `VariablesRef`, coding-scheme, and separately uploaded `.itcr.zip` player-resource references across already uploaded workspace files. Starting the root import captures that transitive closure in a new immutable dependency-snapshot ZIP, records exact member lineage, selects the snapshot in Angular, and runs the normal importer; the original resource-package gate proves the resulting participant download in memory, file, and SQLite stores. Ambiguous references produce structured diagnostics with one Angular action per exact candidate. The chosen source-package ID is validated server-side, retained across later ambiguity decisions, and captured with the remaining unique dependency closure in the same audited immutable snapshot; incomplete matches still fail explicitly. Snapshot package and assembly evidence are committed together only if the complete source-package/activity revision still matches; otherwise the import or manual assembly returns a retryable conflict without leaving a partial aggregate. The sequential loose-file queue exposes its processed count, exact current file, accessible determinate progress, and workspace-refresh phase while disabling duplicate submission; successful files enter reviewed assembly immediately and the final best-effort report remains itemized. Manual assembly remains as the controlled fallback for deliberate 2–100-file composition, rejecting missing documents, unsafe relative paths, duplicate selection ids, case-insensitive duplicate archive paths, and per-file/aggregate size overflow while preserving an existing manifest or generating compatible IMS aliases from paths, original XML metadata, and Verona JSON-LD module identity/version metadata\n - prebuilt ZIP validation rejects case-insensitive duplicate IMS manifest resource identifiers before references are resolved, preventing a later declaration from silently replacing or ambiguously shadowing an earlier Booklet, Unit, coding-scheme, or asset target. Generated assembly manifests apply the same identity rule while deduplicating aliases that resolve to the same selected file\n","move_path":null}},"status":"completed","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nM /Users/julian/code/testcenter-rewrite/rewrite-app/README.md\nM /Users/julian/code/testcenter-rewrite/rewrite-app/docs/PARITY.md\n"},"completed_at_ms":1788803266914}}
