{"timestamp":"2026-09-08T01:41:44.394Z","ordinal":60122,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a07ead-a54a-78a1-bffd-73686d5fcc9b","call_id":"call_IDmJZMvdf4hmNnJ8Evj3mT34","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.2 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"10e399\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.008989708,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":16813,\"output\":\"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 16813)\\nTotal output lines: 207\\n\\n/Users/julian/.zprofile:source:8: no such file or directory: /Users/julian/.bashrc\\nREADME.md:7:link, restart behavior, and verification commands, see\\nREADME.md:138:migration preview includes original view, column, auto-next, and filter settings\\nREADME.md:244:application restarts.\\nREADME.md:272:npm run ci:browser:review\\nREADME.md:278:The browser groups build once and then reuse built artifacts: `ci:browser:quick` covers content, roster links, participant entry, and activation roster warnings; `ci:browser:review` covers response/review handoff paths; `ci:browser:monitor` covers confirmed monitor batch commands, open-run synchronization, and activation-blocking runtime handoff; `ci:browser:ops` covers destructive operator actions and protected-operator auth.\\nREADME.md:291:- browser-driven Angular UI smokes against SQLite in focused content, participant-entry, activation-roster-warning, review-readiness, open-run, monitor-detail, destructive-action, full, and protected operator modes, plus a Postgres-backed protected UI smoke in the Postgres CI matrix\\nREADME.md:329:The public challenge is signed, short-lived, bound to the exact credential input through a keyed digest, and contains no plaintext password or second code. Angular solves it in Web Workers with the same `altcha-lib` mechanism used by Testcenter 18.2. A valid solution is atomically consumed by memory, file, SQLite, or Postgres storage before authentication, so it cannot be replayed across requests, processes, or restarts; rejected or missing proof does not advance the existing login-failure sink. `/diagnostics/config` and runtime preflight expose only the non-secret algorithm, limits, enabled scopes, current key ID, and whether a previous key is configured.\\nREADME.md:414:first sign-in, stop the bootstrap overlay and restart the normal production\\nREADME.md:578:- `GET /api/v1/tenants/{tenantKey}/workspaces/{workspaceKey}/reviews`\\nREADME.md:579:- `POST /api/v1/tenants/{tenantKey}/workspaces/{workspaceKey}/reviews`\\nREADME.md:580:- `PATCH /api/v1/tenants/{tenantKey}/workspaces/{workspaceKey}/reviews/{reviewId}`\\nREADME.md:581:- `DELETE /api/v1/tenants/{tenantKey}/workspaces/{workspaceKey}/reviews/{reviewId}`\\nREADME.md:588:- `GET /api/v1/tenants/{tenantKey}/workspaces/{workspaceKey}/exports/reviews.csv`\\nREADME.md:600:- `GET /api/v1/participant/test-runs/{testRunId}/reviews`\\nREADME.md:601:- `POST /api/v1/participant/test-runs/{testRunId}/reviews`\\nREADME.md:602:- `PATCH /api/v1/participant/test-runs/{testRunId}/reviews/{reviewId}`\\nREADME.md:603:- `DELETE /api/v1/participant/test-runs/{testRunId}/reviews/{reviewId}`\\nREADME.md:604:- `GET /api/v1/participant/sessions/{participantSessionId}/exports/reviews.csv`\\nREADME.md:637:Original review surface: it lists every captured computer/browser, network, and\\nREADME.md:680:- protected admin directory reads are filterable by username, status, role, tenant/workspace scope, and limit so platform operators can narrow user-management follow-up without leaving the shell, with a matching CSV export for access reviews\\nREADME.md:685:- participant review routes are bound to an opaque participant run, reject execution modes without `canReview`, and expose only that run's own test-, unit-, and task/page-level comments; Original Testcenter page/page-label metadata, priorities `0–3`, and simultaneous `tech`/`content`/`design` categories survive create, edit, storage, filtering, and reload. Review-capable sessions also expose the Original starter action `Reviews downloaden`: the server derives the participant exclusively from the opaque session, returns `204` with the original `Keine Kommentare verfügbar.` feedback when no comments exist, and otherwise downloads the participant-isolated Original-compatible semicolon/BOM CSV as `testcenter-reviews.csv`\\nREADME.md:690:- study monitor summary returns workspace-wide group, booklet, and unit progress with authored group labels plus stable keys, participant sessions, saved-roster expected/not-started participants for groups and booklets, roster-derived missing unit expectations, prioritized attention items, latest run states, response counts, review counts, and latest activity timestamps\\nREADME.md:691:- study monitor group detail drills into one group with participant sessions, saved roster entries, status counts, latest runs, response counts, review counts, and per-run context for operator follow-up\\nREADME.md:692:- study monitor booklet detail drills into one booklet with saved roster entries, attached runs, status pressure, unit coverage, response counts, and review counts\\nREADME.md:693:- study monitor participant detail drills into one login with saved roster context, sessions, runs, unit answer status, response counts, and review counts\\nREADME.md:694:- study monitor participant matrix read model exposes participant-by-unit session/run/answer/review status directly for the operator shell\\nREADME.md:696:- study monitor participant matrix CSV export flattens participant-by-unit progress with session/run status, expected/answered flags, response lengths, review counts, and roster display context, and can be narrowed by the same login/group/booklet/unit/status/answer/limit filters used by the operator matrix\\nREADME.md:697:- study monitor run-detail CSV export flattens the selected run into unit rows with expected/current/answered state, response length, review count, and response text for per-participant support handoff\\nREADME.md:702:- ambiguous loose-file dependency imports expose an opaque `dependencySelectionRevision` with their advertised candidates. Guided retries must echo that revision together with `dependencySourcePackageIds`; any intervening workspace-file mutation returns a failed import with `source_document_workspace_dependency_selection_stale`, requiring a fresh candidate review before immutable assembly. The final automatic or manually reviewed ZIP plus its lineage event are reserved atomically against that same complete workspace revision in every store, so a concurrent upload, replacement, deletion, or competing assembly cannot commit a stale or duplicate dependency snapshot\\nREADME.md:708:- participant-session detail now resolves one session together with its content release, full run history, response counts, review counts, and attached review context\\nREADME.md:711:- result-group administration reproduces the Original Testcenter's operator summary with started booklets, per-run minimum/maximum/average answered-unit counts, latest test activity, and response/review/log totals; one group can seed the detailed inspection scopes, while a separate multi-selection supports select-all, individual CSV exports, a combined Original-compatible ZIP with response/log/review CSV and JSON reports plus manifest, and workspace-key-confirmed aggregate deletion with an audit record. Response, review, and log reads accept repeated `groupKey` parameters without breaking the existing single-group filters; exports are explicitly bounded while interactive lists remain capped at 500 rows\\nREADME.md:712:- admin account status management supports a bounded exact multi-selection with current/target-state preview, protects the signed-in account from selection, confirmation-gates the mutation, and reports per-account best-effort successes or stable failures while every update remains independently constrained and audited by the existing platform/tenant/workspace delegation boundary\\nREADME.md:714:- review comments let participants and operators attach, edit, list, delete, and export reviewer notes for concrete test runs, units, or labeled tasks/pages, including original priority and multi-category metadata; review reads are filterable by login, group, booklet, session, run, unit, reviewer, category, and limit, while runtime/workspace cards expose task targets, priorities, and every selected category. The runtime shell also derives a review-readiness checklist that joins answered units, missing responses, unit-level reviews, and whole-run reviews for the selected participant run, and its cards can seed matching response/review filters for follow-up inspection\\nREADME.md:715:- Original Unit attachment variables with `format=\\\"capture-image\\\"` survive packaged XML import and become requested image slots for each started run. The protected Attachment Manager lists missing/captured slots with participant and content context, constrains group monitors to assigned groups, accepts both JSON/Base64 and the original capture client's binary-safe multipart upload, magic-byte-checks PNG/JPEG files up to 10 MiB, previews and deletes durable images, records upload/delete activity, and exposes a stable copyable handoff code. Operators can download one selected or up to 500 role-scoped A4 QR pages with the original configurable label placeholders. A separate mobile `/attachment-capture` route completes the original handoff: an authenticated operator can scan the printed QR code with the rear camera or a saved QR image, switch cameras or flash, use the manual code fallback, verify the server-scoped participant/booklet/unit/variable target, capture an A4-centered camera frame or device photo, preview it, and confirm the upload. The route never turns the QR value into public authority; every lookup and upload reuses the existing role, group, workspace, and read-write checks\\nREADME.md:716:- group result deletion removes collected test runs for one group, reports deleted runs/responses/reviews/logs, records a workspace activity event, refreshes the result inventory, and the frontend requires operators to type the target group key before issuing the destructive action\\nREADME.md:719:- review CSV export returns persisted comments with participant, run, booklet, unit, page, page label, reviewer, priority, category list, compatibility category text, timestamp, and saved-roster display/assignment context, using the same filters as review reads\\nREADME.md:721:- content-release activation readiness now previews whether a staged release can…11813 tokens truncated…code/testcenter/backend/test/unit/controller/SessionControllerTest.php:370:    $loginToken = new AuthToken('login_token', 1, 'login', 1, 'run-hot-return', 'sample_group');\\n/Users/julian/code/testcenter/backend/test/unit/controller/SessionControllerTest.php:398:          'run-hot-return',\\n/Users/julian/code/testcenter/backend/test/unit/controller/SessionControllerTest.php:413:    $personToken = new AuthToken('person_token', 1, 'person', 1, 'run-hot-return', 'sample_group');\\n/Users/julian/code/testcenter/backend/test/unit/dao/AdminDAOTest.php:347:        'mode' => 'run-hot-return',\\n/Users/julian/code/testcenter/backend/test/unit/dao/AdminDAOTest.php:365:        'mode' => 'run-hot-return',\\n/Users/julian/code/testcenter/backend/test/initialization/tests/12.3.3/login_name_spelling.sh:17:echo \\\"<Testtakers><Metadata><Description>UC</Description></Metadata><Group id=\\\\\\\"X\\\\\\\" label=\\\\\\\"x\\\\\\\"><Login mode=\\\\\\\"run-hot-restart\\\\\\\" name=\\\\\\\"x\\\\\\\"><Booklet>BOOKLET.SAMPLE-1</Booklet></Login></Group></Testtakers>\\\" > vo_data/ws_1/Testtakers/uc.xml\\n/Users/julian/code/testcenter/backend/test/initialization/tests/12.3.3/login_name_spelling.sh:18:echo \\\"<Testtakers><Metadata><Description>UC</Description></Metadata><Group id=\\\\\\\"x\\\\\\\" label=\\\\\\\"x\\\\\\\"><Login mode=\\\\\\\"run-hot-restart\\\\\\