{"timestamp":"2026-09-08T02:30:28.434Z","ordinal":60649,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a07cfb-af30-7a62-8a81-f821103d611a","turn_id":"01a07eda-0998-7213-a0bd-4bc585408ed2","item":{"type":"WebSearch","id":"exec-bb758372-561a-4a61-b09f-d856601e0502","query":"site.docs.entire.io checkpoints commits session attach ...","action":{"type":"search","queries":["site.docs.entire.io checkpoints commits session attach","site:docs.entire.io checkpoint commit session"]},"results":[{"type":"text_result","domain":"docs.entire.io","ref_id":"turn0search0","snippet":"Entire integrates with AI coding agents by installing lifecycle hooks that capture each session and link it to your Git history.When you commit, Entire writes","title":"Overview - Entire","url":"https://docs.entire.io/agents/overview"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"docs.entire.io","ref_id":"turn0search1","snippet":"Entire captures that context as Checkpoints: versioned records of agent-assisted changes, linked to Git so you can trace any commit back to the session that","title":"Overview - Entire","url":"https://docs.entire.io/overview"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"docs.entire.io","ref_id":"turn0search2","snippet":"`entire checkpoint explain --generate` (on-demand AI summary) | Whichever provider is configured via `summary_generation.provider` — typically the same agent that ran the session, e.g. ...","title":"Security & Privacy - Entire","url":"https://docs.entire.io/security"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"docs.entire.io","ref_id":"turn0search3","snippet":"Checkpoint Creation — created when you or the agent make a Git commit. ... Use `entire checkpoint rewind` to restore to a previous checkpoint during","title":"Copilot CLI - Entire","url":"https://docs.entire.io/agents/copilot-cli"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"docs.entire.io","ref_id":"turn0search4","snippet":"Timestamps | Session, message, and checkpoint timing ... Inspect any commit or checkpoint with `entire checkpoint explain`.","title":"Cursor - Entire","url":"https://docs.entire.io/agents/cursor"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"entire.io","ref_id":"turn0search5","snippet":"While that future is in flight, we focused on a few key improvements this week: a new repository overview page on entire.io, updates to the","title":"Entire Dispatch 0x0008","url":"https://entire.io/blog/entire-dispatch-0x0008"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"docs.entire.io","ref_id":"turn0search6","snippet":"Use `entire checkpoint rewind` to restore to a previous checkpoint during or after a Codex session. ... Inspect any commit or checkpoint with `entire checkpoint","title":"Codex - Entire","url":"https://docs.entire.io/agents/codex"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"github.com","ref_id":"turn0search7","snippet":"This document describes the git-branch layout; for the ref-based backend — its ref naming, sharding, push/fetch model, read routing, and configuration — see Ref-Based Checkpoint","title":"cli/docs/architecture/sessions-and-checkpoints.md at main · entireio/cli · GitHub","url":"https://github.com/entireio/cli/blob/main/docs/architecture/sessions-and-checkpoints.md"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"github.com","ref_id":"turn0search8","snippet":"scoop bucket add entire https://github.com/entireio/scoop-bucket.git ... `entire checkpoint explain` | Explain a session, commit, or checkpoint ... `entire session attach` | Attach to a previously","title":"GitHub - entireio/cli: 📜 Entire CLI hooks into your Git workflow to capture AI agent sessions as you work. Sessions are indexed alongside commits, creating a searchable record of how code was written in your repo. · GitHub","url":"https://github.com/entireio/cli"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"docs.entire.io","ref_id":"turn0search9","snippet":"Timestamps | Session, message, and checkpoint timing ... Inspect any commit or checkpoint with `entire checkpoint explain`.","title":"Factory Droid - Entire","url":"https://docs.entire.io/agents/factory-droid"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"entire.io","ref_id":"turn0search10","snippet":"A new getting started flow guides you through four steps to set up Entire and create your first checkpoint.The flow stays in the app header","title":"Set Up Entire Without Hunting for the Next Command","url":"https://entire.io/blog/entire-dispatch-0x001b"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"entire.io","ref_id":"turn0search11","snippet":"Capture every agent session alongside your commits. ... >entire repo mirror create entireio/cli ... Every clone carries its checkpoints and session history at shallow-clone speed.","title":"Entire CLI","url":"https://entire.io/about/cli"}]},"completed_at_ms":1788834628434}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-08T02:30:28.441Z","ordinal":60650,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a07eda-4359-7933-b194-742db217a346","call_id":"call_IwO5UVJgxAhl19nN52LuIxoq","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 3.7 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"cf6f6d\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.139544,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":483,\"output\":\"/Users/julian/.zprofile:source:8: no such file or directory: /Users/julian/.bashrc\\n5bd7c13 Preserve participant responses when returning from test completion\\n\\nb51c0f0 Make fresh local demos reproducible and await IB state parts\\nEntire-Checkpoint: 01M1Z92Z1Y7FKE5ZH6JXY2YMNE\\n\\n634189c Guard source package assembly races\\nEntire-Checkpoint: 01M1W3X3RVDCK2XC818BZY6R9Y\\n\\n02b62dd Fix review code notice reactivity\\nEntire-Checkpoint: 01M1W3X3RVDCK2XC818BZY6R9Y\\n\\nede5271 Match review code notice dismissal\\nEntire-Checkpoint: 01M1W3X3RVDCK2XC818BZY6R9Y\\n\\nd374fb1 Use load state for participant reload gate\\nEntire-Checkpoint: 01M1W3X3RVDCK2XC818BZY6R9Y\\n\\n56f231b Stabilize Verona and outbox browser gates\\nEntire-Checkpoint: 01M1W3X3RVDCK2XC818BZY6R9Y\\n\\n9abcc9a Audit parity against Testcenter 18.3\\n\\n8220675 Verify replacement chain rollback lineage\\nEntire-Checkpoint: 01M1W3X3RVDCK2XC818BZY6R9Y\\n\\n9d994a9 Allow slow cold compose installs to finish\\nEntire-Checkpoint: 01M17MBK5MJ164DHNDD9Y0B73E\\n\\norigin\\thttps://github.com/jurei733/testcenter-rewrite.git (fetch)\\norigin\\thttps://github.com/jurei733/testcenter-rewrite.git (push)\\n● Enabled · branch testcenter-rewrite-parity\\n  Agents · Codex\\n  Checkpoints sync to: origin\\n  1 checkpoint not yet on origin — it syncs with your next 'git push origin'\\nAgents: run `entire agent-help` for machine-readable usage.\\nrefs/entire/checkpoints/3E/01M17MBK5MJ164DHNDD9Y0B73E\\nrefs/entire/checkpoints/9Y/01M1W3X3RVDCK2XC818BZY6R9Y\\nrefs/entire/checkpoints/NE/01M1Z92Z1Y7FKE5ZH6JXY2YMNE\\n4:applies_to: cwd=/Users/julian/code/testcenter-rewrite/rewrite-app; reuse_rule=reuse implementation and handoff guidance in this checkout; commits, CI runs, Entire checkpoints, and parity status are snapshots that must be rechecked.\\n45:- 01a07cfb-af30-7a62-8a81-f821103d611a, Testcenter Rewrite auf 100 Prozent, GPT-6 Astra, npm run start:local, http://127.0.0.1:4310/app, Entire, 01M1W3X3RVDCK2XC818BZY6R9Y, P0, Verona\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Overview - Entire (https://docs.entire.io/agents/overview)\nciteturn0search0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 months ago; Entire integrates with AI coding agents by installing lifecycle hooks that capture each session and link it to your Git history.When you commit, Entire writes a checkpoint with the full transcript, file changes, tokens, and tool calls to the `entire/checkpoints/v1` branch — no extra commits on your working branch.\n\n# Overview\n\nSet up Entire with your AI coding agent — supported integrations and how to add your own\n\nCopy page\n\n> ## Documentation Index\n> \n> Fetch the complete documentation index at: https://docs.entire.io/llms.txt\n> \n> Use this file to discover all available pages before exploring further.\n\nEntire integrates with AI coding agents by installing lifecycle hooks that capture each session and link it to your Git history. When you commit, Entire writes a checkpoint with the full transcript, file changes, tokens, and tool calls to the `entire/checkpoints/v1` branch — no extra commits on your working branch. The default agent is Claude Code. To choose a different one, run `entire agent add <name>`.\n\n\nBuilt-in agents\n\n  * Claude Code — Stable · `--agent claude-code`. Full feature support including nested subagent capture.\n  * Codex — Stable · `--agent codex`. Native hook system; main session capture (no subagent hooks yet).\n  * Copilot CLI — Stable · `--agent copilot-cli`. Native hooks; token usage available post-session.\n  * Cursor — Stable · `--agent cursor`. IDE and CLI. Rewind and resume are not available.\n  * Factory Droid — Stable · `--agent factoryai-droid`. Subagent-aware capture via `pre-tool-use` and `post-tool-use` hooks.\n  * Gemini CLI — Stable · `--agent gemini`. File changes captured; conversation transcript and token tracking are limited.\n  * OpenCode — Stable · `--agent opencode`. TypeScript plugin integration; supports mid-turn commits.\n  * Pi — Preview · `--agent pi`. TypeScript extension integration with JSONL transcript and token capture.\n\nDon't see your agent?\n\nAny agent can be added by writing an executable named `entire-agent-<name>` and placing it on your `$PATH`. The Entire CLI auto-discovers it. Working examples at github.com/entireio/external-agents.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nOverview - Entire (https://docs.entire.io/overview)\nciteturn0search1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 months ago; Entire captures that context as Checkpoints: versioned records of agent-assisted changes, linked to Git so you can trace any commit back to the session that produced it.\n\n# Overview\n\nGit shows what changed. Entire shows why.\n\nCopy page\n\n> ## Documentation Index\n> \n> Fetch the complete documentation index at: https://docs.entire.io/llms.txt\n> \n> Use this file to discover all available pages before exploring further.\n\nEntire is a new, CLI-first system of record that captures the context behind agent-assisted code changes.\n\n## \n\n​\n\nWhy Entire exists\n\nWhen an AI agent writes code, the commit diff often leaves out the most important context:\n\n  * what prompt started the work,\n  * what files the agent inspected,\n  * what tools it ran,\n  * what alternatives it tried,\n  * and why the final approach was chosen.\nEntire captures that context as Checkpoints: versioned records of agent-assisted changes, linked to Git so you can trace any commit back to the session that produced it. With Entire, you can:\n\n  * Review the prompt, transcript, and tool calls behind a commit, not just the diff.\n  * Rewind to earlier Checkpoints in an agent session.\n  * Search every prompt and session across a repository.\n  * Continue from prior agent sessions instead of starting cold.\n\n\nParts of Entire\n\nEntire has two surfaces:\n\nEntire CLI\n\nEntire CLI runs locally in your Git repository, installs hooks for Git and supported agents, captures sessions in the background, and links Checkpoints to your commits.\n\nEntire.io\n\nEntire.io provides the web interface for exploring the history captured by the CLI.\n\n\nGet started\n\nEntire works with the tools developers already use for agentic coding.\n\n## Claude Code\n\nCapture Claude Code sessions and Checkpoints.\n\n## Codex\n\nCapture Codex CLI sessions and Checkpoints.\n\n## Cursor\n\nCapture Cursor agent sessions and Checkpoints.\n\n## Copilot CLI\n\nCapture Copilot CLI sessions and Checkpoints.\n\n## Gemini CLI\n\nCapture Gemini CLI sessions and Checkpoints.\n\n## OpenCode\n\nCapture OpenCode sessions and Checkpoints.\n\n## Factory Droid\n\nCapture Factory Droid sessions and Checkpoints.\n\n## External agents\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSecurity & Privacy - Entire (https://docs.entire.io/security)\nciteturn0search2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 months ago; `entire checkpoint explain --generate` (on-demand AI summary)  | Whichever provider is configured via `summary_generation.provider` — typically the same agent that ran the session, e.g. ... Checkpoint commit signing\nExternal agent plugins. Plugins are arbitrary executables on `$PATH` that the CLI invokes during agent sessions. They have the same filesystem access as the CLI itself. Only install plugins you trust. See External Agent Plugins for the protocol; the security warning there applies fully.\n\nCheckpoint commit signing\n\nCheckpoint commits (on the shadow branch and the metadata branch) can be GPG- or SSH-signed using the same key already configured for your regular Git commits.Requirements (all of these must be true):\n\n  1. `commit.gpgsign = true` is set in your global or system Git config.\n  2. A supported signer is available — GPG (default) or SSH (set `gpg.format = ssh` and run `ssh-agent`).\n  3. The Entire setting `sign_checkpoint_commits` is `true` (the default; defaults to true when unset).\nBest-effort behavior. Signing never blocks a commit. If the signer is unavailable, fails, or your hardware token requires a touch you didn’t give, the commit is created unsigned and a warning is logged to `.entire/logs/`. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCopilot CLI - Entire (https://docs.entire.io/agents/copilot-cli)\nciteturn0search3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 months ago; Checkpoint Creation — created when you or the agent make a Git commit. ... Use `entire checkpoint rewind` to restore to a previous checkpoint during or after a Copilot CLI session.\n  2. Turn Tracking — each prompt and agent response is captured via hooks.\n  3. Checkpoint Creation — created when you or the agent make a Git commit.\n  4. Transcript Capture — session transcripts are read from Copilot CLI’s JSONL event log.\n  5. Session Storage — data saved to the `entire/checkpoints/v1` branch.\n\nWhat gets captured\n\nData  | Description\n--- | ---\nConversation  | Full transcript of prompts and responses\nFile changes  | All files modified during the session\nToken usage  | Input, output, and cache tokens\nTimestamps  | Session and checkpoint timing\nCheckpoints  | Rewind points within sessions\n\nFeatures\n\nRewind during sessions. Use `entire checkpoint rewind` to restore to a previous checkpoint during or after a Copilot CLI session. See the `rewind` command reference for full flag documentation.Resume previous sessions. Switch to a session’s branch with `entire session resume <branch>`. The CLI restores the session log if needed and prints `copilot --resume <sessionId>`. See the `resume` command reference for full flag documentation.Explain commits. \nExample workflow\n    \n    `# 1. Setup\n    cd my-project\n    entire agent add copilot-cli\n    \n    # 2. Start Copilot CLI\n    copilot\n    \n    # 3. Work with Copilot\n    # Ask it to write code, make changes, etc.\n    \n    # 4. Check session (in another terminal)\n    entire status\n    \n    # 5. Rewind if needed\n    entire checkpoint rewind\n    \n    # 6. Commit when ready\n    git add .\n    git commit -m \"Add feature with Copilot\"\n    \n    # 7. Push to see on entire.io\n    git push\n    `\n\nTroubleshooting\n\nSession not detected\n\n  1. Ensure you’re in an Entire-enabled repo: `entire status`\n  2. Verify hooks are installed: check `.github/hooks/entire.json` exists\n  3. Make sure Copilot CLI is running from within the repository\n  4. Run `entire agent add copilot-cli` to reinstall hooks\n\nNo checkpoints created\n\n  1. Checkpoints require file changes\n  2. Make sure Copilot is modifying files in the repository\n  3. Check your settings in `.entire/settings.json`\n\nTranscript not captured\n\n  1. Verify Copilot CLI is writing events to `~/.copilot/session-state/`\n  2. Check that the session has a valid `events.jsonl` file\n  3. Token usage is only fully available after the session ends--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCursor - Entire (https://docs.entire.io/agents/cursor)\nciteturn0search4 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 months ago; Timestamps  | Session, message, and checkpoint timing ... Inspect any commit or checkpoint with `entire checkpoint explain`.\n--- | ---\nConversation  | Full transcript of prompts and responses\nFile changes  | All files modified during the session\nSubagent calls  | Nested agent invocations and operations\nTimestamps  | Session, message, and checkpoint timing\n\nUnlike Claude Code, Cursor transcripts do not include token usage data or detailed tool invocation records.\n\nFeatures\n\nSession capture. Entire automatically captures the conversation flow and file modifications when Cursor launches. Run `entire status` from a separate terminal to see active sessions.Explain commits. Inspect any commit or checkpoint with `entire checkpoint explain`. See the `explain` command reference for full flag documentation.Rewind and resume are not supported — see the warning above and the caveats below.\n\nCaveats and limitations\n\nNo rewind or resume. Cannot restore to previous checkpoints; cannot resume previous sessions.No token accounting. Cursor transcripts do not include token usage data (unlike Claude Code). You can still see the conversation and file changes, but not the computational cost.File detection via `git status`. Especially important since rewind is not available.Review sessions in PRs. Commits include `Entire-Checkpoint` trailers. Reviewers can click through to view session details — understanding why code was written helps with review.\n\nExample workflow\n\nWith Cursor IDE:\n    \n    `# 1. Enable Entire\n    cd my-project\n    entire agent add cursor\n    \n    # 2. Start Cursor IDE\n    cursor\n    \n    # 3. Work with Cursor IDE\n    # Use @ mentions to attach files for context\n    # Ask the AI to implement features\n    \n    # 4. Check status (in another terminal)\n    entire status\n    \n    # 5. Commit when ready\n    git add .\n    git commit -m \"Add feature with Cursor\"\n    \n    # 6. Push to see on entire.io\n    git push\n    `\n\nWith Cursor CLI:\n    \n    `# 1. Enable Entire\n    cd my-project\n    entire agent add cursor\n    \n    # 2. Run Cursor CLI\n    agent\n    \n    # 2.1 Instruct Cursor CLI\n    \"refactor the authentication module\"\n    \n    # 3. In parallel terminal, run another Cursor CLI\n    agent\n    \n    # 3.1 Instruct the other CLI\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nEntire Dispatch 0x0008 (https://entire.io/blog/entire-dispatch-0x0008)\nciteturn0search5 [wordlim: 200] Published: 5 months ago; Crawled: 5 days ago; While that future is in flight, we focused on a few key improvements this week: a new repository overview page on entire.io, updates to the Entire CLI in v0.5.3, and the release of go-git/v6. ...     * Total number of commits, and total commits with Checkpoints attached ...   * Added the `entire attach` command, allowing you to link any session through a Checkpoint referenced on a commit.\n    * Opened and merged PRs\n\nRepository overview page\n\n## Entire CLI Updates\n\n### Session Management Enhancements\n\n  * We introduced new `entire sessions` subcommands in the Entire CLI:\n    * `entire sessions list` - enabling you to view sessions\n    * `entire sessions info <session-id>` - to inspect session details\n    * `entire sessions stop [session-id]` - to terminate stuck sessions\n\nNote: `entire sessions stop` is a temporary stop-gap while we work toward automatically detecting and flagging stuck sessions, reducing the need for manual intervention.\n\n### Manual Session Linking with `entire attach`\n\n  * Added the `entire attach` command, allowing you to link any session through a Checkpoint referenced on a commit. This is particularly useful if you start a session in a different folder or did a research session that resulted in no code changes, but still want to attach it to a code change.\n\n### Authentication for Checkpoints\n\n  * Added `ENTIRE_CHECKPOINT_TOKEN` environment variable, enabling separate authentication for interacting with a remote Checkpoints repository.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCodex - Entire (https://docs.entire.io/agents/codex)\nciteturn0search6 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 months ago; Use `entire checkpoint rewind` to restore to a previous checkpoint during or after a Codex session. ... Inspect any commit or checkpoint with `entire checkpoint explain`.\nThe hooks track the session lifecycle:\n\n  1. Session Start — `SessionStart` creates a new Entire session.\n  2. Prompt Tracking — `UserPromptSubmit` captures each user prompt.\n  3. Turn Completion — `Stop` finalizes each turn and advances checkpoint state.\n  4. Transcript Capture — Entire reads Codex’s JSONL rollout transcript from `~/.codex/` or `CODEX_HOME`.\n  5. Session Storage — data is saved to the `entire/checkpoints/v1` branch.\n\nWhat gets captured\n\nData  | Description\n--- | ---\nConversation  | Full transcript of prompts and responses\nFile changes  | Files modified via `apply_patch` in Codex rollouts\nToken usage  | Input, cached-input, output, and reasoning tokens\nTimestamps  | Session, turn, and checkpoint timing\n\nFeatures\n\nRewind during sessions. Use `entire checkpoint rewind` to restore to a previous checkpoint during or after a Codex session. When you rewind, Entire restores the checkpointed transcript state and shows the command to continue the Codex session. See the `rewind` command reference for full flag documentation.Resume previous sessions. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\ncli/docs/architecture/sessions-and-checkpoints.md at main · entireio/cli · GitHub (https://github.com/entireio/cli/blob/main/docs/architecture/sessions-and-checkpoints.md)\nciteturn0search7 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; This document describes the git-branch layout; for the ref-based backend — its ref naming, sharding, push/fetch model, read routing, and configuration — see Ref-Based Checkpoint Backend. ... In session metadata, `checkpoints_count` is the displayed prompt-window count for that session. `save_step_count` records SaveStep-created shadow-branch commits and is the conservative \"real checkpoint work happened\" signal; it is omitted when zero (for example, commit-only/fallback sessions). `save_step_count` is not aggregated into the root `CheckpointSummary`. ... Checkpoints written by `entire import <agent>` additionally carry a `commit_sha` (omitempty) on both the session `Metadata` and the root `CheckpointSummary`, set to the default branch's head at import time — origin's tip is preferred (the commit the server already knows about), falling back to the local branch tip, then HEAD, then empty when nothing resolves. ... Explicit checkpoint-data writers such as `entire session attach`, `entire checkpoint explain --generate`, and `entire import <agent>` fail when the local policy cannot be satisfied.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nGitHub - entireio/cli: 📜 Entire CLI hooks into your Git workflow to capture AI agent sessions as you work. Sessions are indexed alongside commits, creating a searchable record of how code was written in your repo. · GitHub (https://github.com/entireio/cli)\nciteturn0search8 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 months ago;     scoop bucket add entire https://github.com/entireio/scoop-bucket.git ... `entire checkpoint explain`  | Explain a session, commit, or checkpoint ... `entire session attach`  | Attach to a previously detached session ... `--checkpoint-remote <provider:owner/repo>`  | Push checkpoint branches to a separate repo (e.g., `github:org/checkpoints-repo`)\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nFactory Droid - Entire (https://docs.entire.io/agents/factory-droid)\nciteturn0search9 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 months ago; Timestamps  | Session, message, and checkpoint timing ... Inspect any commit or checkpoint with `entire checkpoint explain`.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSet Up Entire Without Hunting for the Next Command (https://entire.io/blog/entire-dispatch-0x001b)\nciteturn0search10 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2 weeks ago; Crawled: 5 days ago; A new getting started flow guides you through four steps to set up Entire and create your first checkpoint.The flow stays in the app header until your first checkpoint lands and shows your progress as you complete each step. ...   * Install the CLI: run `curl -fsSL https://entire.io/install.sh | bash`, or install with Homebrew. ... Your session history stays attached to the commit it belongs to, so the agent work behind a change is there when you look for it.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nEntire CLI (https://entire.io/about/cli)\nciteturn0search11 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Capture every agent session alongside your commits. ... >entire repo mirror create entireio/cli ... Every clone carries its checkpoints and session history at shallow-clone speed.\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a07eda-0998-7213-a0bd-4bc585408ed2","create_time":1788834628.441451}}}
