{"timestamp":"2026-09-08T02:33:49.930Z","ordinal":60685,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a07edd-5669-7de1-a0a9-ff8aadb1f68b","call_id":"call_pVgvitbAEViFAUQ5oXJPZBZ9","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 1.8 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Codex Meetups | OpenAI Developers (https://developers.openai.com/community/meetups)\nciteturn1search0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; # Codex Meetups\n\n# Codex Meetups\n\nMeetups hosted by Codex community & OpenAI.\n\n[Button: Upcoming][Button: Past]\n\n7 events\n\nLocation All locations[Input]\n\nDate All dates[Input]\n\nImage: Stylized city cover for Kuala Lumpur\n\nUpcoming Sep 9\n\nCommunity Hackathon\n\n### Kuala Lumpur, Malaysia\n\nSeptember 9, 2026\n\nHosted by Siow Yen Chong\n\nRegister now (opens in a new tab)Share city\n\nImage: Stylized city cover for Perth\n\nUpcoming Sep 10\n\nCommunity Meetup\n\n### Perth, Australia\n\nSeptember 10, 2026\n\nHosted by Jia Keatnuxsuo\n\nRegister now (opens in a new tab)Share city\n\nImage: Stylized city cover for Singapore\n\nUpcoming Sep 12\n\nCommunity Hackathon\n\n### Singapore\n\nSeptember 12, 2026\n\nHosted by Son Le Thanh\n\nRegister now (opens in a new tab)Share city\n\nImage: Stylized city cover for Antwerp\n\nUpcoming Sep 16\n\nCommunity Hackathon\n\n### Antwerp, Belgium\n\nSeptember 16, 2026\n\nHosted by Oleksandr Tsepukh\n\nRegister now (opens in a new tab)Share city\n\nImage: Stylized city cover for Goiânia\n\nUpcoming Sep 19\n\nCommunity Meetup\n\n### Goiânia, Brazil\n\nSeptember 19, 2026\n\nHosted by Guilherme Tavares\n\nRegister now (opens in a new tab)Share city\n\nImage: Stylized city cover for Perth\n\nUpcoming Sep 19\n\nCommunity Meetup\n\n### Perth, Australia\n\nSeptember 19, 2026\n\nHosted by Jia Keatnuxsuo\n\nRegister now (opens in a new tab)Share city\n\nImage: Stylized city cover for Adelaide\n\nUpcoming Sep 24\n\nCommunity Hackathon\n\n### Adelaide, Australia\n\nSeptember 24, 2026\n\nHosted by Matthew McKinlay\n\nRegister now (opens in a new tab)Share city\n\n## Host a meetup\n\nWant to host a Codex community meetup in your city? Learn about the Codex Ambassadors program. Applications are currently paused, and we plan to open a future cohort later. You can also explore community posts from builders shipping with Codex.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nOpenAI Developers (https://developers.openai.com/)\nciteturn1search1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday; Start building with Astra View model details ... Realtime and audio Codex changelog Community page\nFor the complete documentation index, see llms.txt. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending `.md` to the page URL.\n\n# OpenAI for developers\n\nDocs and resources to help you build with, for, and on OpenAI.\n\nImage\n\n## Introducing GPT-6 Astra\n\nOur most capable model, built for the hardest end-to-end work.\n\nStart building with Astra View model details\n\nAPI Platform Use our APIs and models to build your own AI experiences. Codex Build and ship faster with our coding agent — everywhere you work. Plugins Extend ChatGPT and Codex with skills, MCP servers, and optional UI.\n\n## Codex use cases\n\nLearn how teams are using Codex to automate tasks, build apps and ship with confidence.\n\nExplore use cases (opens in a new tab)\n\nImage: Illustration of Codex workflows and use cases\n\n## Showcase\n\nDiscover what builders are creating with Codex and the OpenAI API, and build your own version.\n\nExplore demos\n\nImage: Illustration of polished OpenAI demo showcases\n\n## Featured\n\nImage\n\n## GPT Image 2 for image generation and editing\n\nGenerate and edit images with stronger instruction following, flexible sizes, and high-fidelity image inputs.\n\nRead the GPT Image 2 prompting guide\n\n### Codex for (almost) everything\n\nApril 16, 2026\n\nRealtime and audio Codex changelog Community page\n\n## Blog posts\n\nView all\n\nBuilding games with Astra How I built a procedural space exploration game in Codex, from concept art to planets you can land on. Sep 4, 2026 Codex Architectural visualization with Astra How I used Astra to design a house, refine its everyday details, and explore it through Blender camera tours and an Unreal Engine 5 walkthrough. Sep 4, 2026 Codex Automating repetitive work at OpenAI with Codex How Runme and WebMCP turn recurring engineering tasks into reviewable, reusable workflows. Aug 25, 2026 Codex\n\nHelp center Frequently asked account and billing questions Developer forum Discuss topics with other developers OpenAI Academy Courses and resources for learning about AI Status Check the status of OpenAI services\n\nAsk AI\n\n## Docs agent\n\nLoading docs agent...--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\ncodex-mini-latest Model | OpenAI API (https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/models/codex-mini-latest)\nciteturn1search2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday; Image: codex-mini-latestcodex-mini-latest ... Text tokens\n\nv1/realtime/transcription_sessions\n\nAssistants\n\nv1/assistants\n\nBatch\n\nv1/batch\n\nFine-tuning\n\nv1/fine-tuning\n\nEmbeddings\n\nv1/embeddings\n\nImage generation\n\nv1/images/generations\n\nVideos\n\nv1/videos\n\nImage edit\n\nv1/images/edits\n\nSpeech generation\n\nv1/audio/speech\n\nTranscription\n\nv1/audio/transcriptions\n\nTranslation\n\nv1/audio/translations\n\n\nFeatures\n\nStreaming\n\nSupported\n\nFunction calling\n\nSupported\n\nStructured outputs\n\nSupported\n\nFine-tuning\n\nNot supported\n\nPredicted outputs\n\nNot supported\n\nSnapshots let you lock in a specific version of the model so that performance and behavior remain consistent. Below is a list of all available snapshots and aliases for codex-mini-latest.\n\nImage: codex-mini-latest\n\ncodex-mini-latest\n\ncodex-mini-latest\n\nDeprecated\n\ncodex-mini-latest\n\nRate limits\n\nRate limits ensure fair and reliable access to the API by placing specific caps on requests, tokens, audio duration, or other usage within a given time period. Your usage tier determines how high these limits are set and automatically increases as you send more requests and spend more on the API.\n\nTier  | RPM  | TPM  | Batch queue limit\n--- | --- | --- | ---\nFree  | Not supported\nTier 1  | 1,000  | 100,000  | 1,000,000\nTier 2  | 2,000  | 200,000  | 2,000,000\nTier 3  | 5,000  | 4,000,000  | 40,000,000\nTier 4  | 10,000  | 10,000,000  | 1,000,000,000\nTier 5  | 30,000  | 150,000,000  | 15,000,000,000--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nGPT-5-Codex Model | OpenAI API (https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/models/gpt-5-codex)\nciteturn1search3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Image: gpt-5-codex ... If you want to learn more about prompting GPT-5-Codex, refer to our dedicated guide. ... Text tokens\n\n$1.25\n\nModalities\n\nText\n\nInput and output\n\nImage\n\nInput only\n\nAudio\n\nNot supported\n\nVideo\n\nNot supported\n\nEndpoints\n\nChat Completions\n\nv1/chat/completions\n\nResponses\n\nv1/responses\n\nRealtime\n\nv1/realtime\n\nRealtime translation\n\nv1/realtime/translations\n\nRealtime transcription\n\nv1/realtime/transcription_sessions\n\nAssistants\n\nv1/assistants\n\nBatch\n\nv1/batch\n\nFine-tuning\n\nv1/fine-tuning\n\nEmbeddings\n\nv1/embeddings\n\nImage generation\n\nv1/images/generations\n\nVideos\n\nv1/videos\n\nImage edit\n\nv1/images/edits\n\nSpeech generation\n\nv1/audio/speech\n\nTranscription\n\nv1/audio/transcriptions\n\nTranslation\n\nv1/audio/translations\n\nModeration\n\nv1/moderations\n\nCompletions (legacy)\n\nv1/completions\n\nFeatures\n\nStreaming\n\nSupported\n\nFunction calling\n\nSupported\n\nStructured outputs\n\nSupported\n\nFine-tuning\n\nNot supported\n\nPredicted outputs\n\nNot supported\n\nSnapshots\n\nSnapshots let you lock in a specific version of the model so that performance and behavior remain consistent. Below is a list of all available snapshots and aliases for GPT-5-Codex.\n\nImage: gpt-5-codex\n\ngpt-5-codex\n\ngpt-5-codex\n\nDeprecated\n\ngpt-5-codex\n\nRate limits\n\nRate limits ensure fair and reliable access to the API by placing specific caps on requests, tokens, audio duration, or other usage within a given time period. Your usage tier determines how high these limits are set and automatically increases as you send more requests and spend more on the API.\n\nTier  | RPM  | TPM  | Batch queue limit\n--- | --- | --- | ---\nFree  | Not supported\nTier 1  | 500  | 500,000  | 1,500,000\nTier 2  | 5,000  | 1,000,000  | 3,000,000\nTier 3  | 5,000  | 2,000,000  | 100,000,000\nTier 4  | 10,000  | 4,000,000  | 200,000,000\nTier 5  | 15,000  | 10,000,000  | 15,000,000,000--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCommunity | OpenAI Developers (https://developers.openai.com/community)\nciteturn1search4 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; > I started a session locally on codex app > had to leave so I handed it off to codex cloud (with 2 attempts) > got back to my computer, compared both attempts, picked the better one, synced it back to my computer > continued to iterate on it locally ... Check GPT-5.4 projects on the Codex App, continue & start new ones 4. ... > I started a session locally on codex app > had to leave so I handed it off to codex cloud (with 2 attempts) > got back to my computer, compared both attempts, picked the better one, synced it back to my computer > continued to iterate on it locally\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nGPT-5.3-Codex Model | OpenAI API (https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/models/gpt-5.3-codex)\nciteturn1search5 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 4 days ago; Image: gpt-5.3-codex ... If you want to learn more about prompting GPT-5.3-Codex, refer to our dedicated guide. ... Text tokens\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nModel guidance | OpenAI API (https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/latest-model)\nciteturn1search6 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Do not stop at acknowledging capability (e.g. ... ## Migration quickstart ... Codex can apply the recommended changes in this guide with the OpenAI Docs skill. ... For Responses, remove `message.output_text.logprobs` from `include`.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCreate completion | OpenAI API Reference (https://developers.openai.com/api/reference/java/resources/completions/methods/create)\nciteturn1search7 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; The returned text will not contain the stop sequence.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nGPT-5.2-Codex Model | OpenAI API (https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/models/gpt-5.2-codex)\nciteturn1search8 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Image: gpt-5.2-codex ... If you want to learn more about prompting GPT-5.2-Codex, refer to our dedicated guide. ... Text tokens\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nAll models | OpenAI API (https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/models/all)\nciteturn1search9 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday; 37†GPT-5.2 Previous flagship model for professional work with configurable reasoning effort】GPT-5.2 Pro Previous pro model for professional work that produces smarter and more precise responses.GPT-5.1 The best model for coding and agentic tasks with configurable reasoning effort GPT-5 Previous intelligent reasoning model for coding and agentic tasks with configurable reasoning effort GPT-5 Mini Strong intelligence for cost sensitive, low latency, high volume workloads GPT-5 nano Fastest, most cost-efficient version of GPT-5 GPT-5 Pro Version of GPT-5 that produces smarter and more precise responses o3-pro Version of o3 with more compute for better responses o3 Reasoning model for complex tasks, succeeded by GPT-5 GPT-4.1 Smartest non-reasoning model GPT-4.1 Mini Smaller, faster version of GPT-4.1 omni-moderation Identify potentially harmful content in text and images GPT-4o Mini Fast, affordable small model for focused tasks GPT-4o Fast, intelligent, flexible GPT model GPT-Realtime Deprecated Model capable of realtime text and audio inputs and outputs GPT-Audio Deprecated For audio inputs and outputs with Chat Completions API GPT-5.3 Chat Deprecated GPT-5.3 Instant model used in ChatGPT GPT-5.2 Chat Deprecated GPT-5.2 model used in ChatGPT GPT-5.2-Codex Deprecated Our most intelligent coding model optimized for long-horizon, agentic coding tasks.Sora 2 Deprecated Flagship video generation with synced audio Sora 2 Pro Deprecated Most advanced synced-audio video generation GPT-Image-1.5 Deprecated Our previous image generation model chatgpt-image-latest Deprecated Previous image model used in ChatGPT.GPT-Image-1 Mini Deprecated A cost-efficient version of GPT Image 1 GPT-Image-1 Deprecated Our previous image generation model o3-deep-research Deprecated Our most powerful deep research model o4-mini-deep-research Deprecated Faster, more affordable deep research model GPT-4.1 nano Deprecated Fastest, most cost-efficient version of GPT-4.1 o4-mini Deprecated Fast, cost-efficient reasoning model, succeeded by GPT-5 Mini o1-pro Deprecated Version of o1 with more compute for better responses computer-use-preview Deprecated Specialized model for computer use tool GPT-Realtime Mini Deprecated A cost-efficient version of GPT-Realtime GPT-Audio Mini Deprecated A cost-efficient version of GPT Audio GPT-4o Mini Search Preview Deprecated Fast, affordable small model for web search GPT-4o Search Preview Deprecated GPT model for web search in Chat Completions GPT-4.5 Preview Deprecated Deprecated large model.o3-mini Deprecated A small model alternative to o3 o1 Deprecated Previous full o-series reasoning model o1-mini Deprecated A small model alternative to o1 o1 Preview Deprecated Preview of our first o-series reasoning model GPT-4o Audio Deprecated GPT-4o models capable of audio inputs and outputs GPT-4o Mini Audio Deprecated Smaller model capable of audio inputs and outputs GPT-4o Mini Realtime Deprecated Smaller realtime model for text and audio inputs and outputs GPT-4o Realtime Deprecated Model capable of realtime text and audio inputs and outputs GPT-4 Turbo Deprecated An older high-intelligence GPT model babbage-002 Deprecated Replacement for the GPT-3 ada and babbage base models ChatGPT-4o Deprecated GPT-4o model used in ChatGPT GPT-5.1-Codex Deprecated A version of GPT-5.1 optimized for agentic coding in Codex.GPT-5.1-Codex-Max Deprecated A version of GPT-5.1-codex optimized for long running tasks.GPT-5.1-Codex Mini Deprecated Smaller, more cost-effective, less-capable version of GPT-5.1-Codex GPT-5-Codex Deprecated A version of GPT-5 optimized for agentic coding in Codex codex-mini-latest Deprecated Fast reasoning model optimized for the Codex CLI davinci-002 Deprecated Replacement for the GPT-3 curie and davinci base models GPT-3.5 Turbo Deprecated Legacy GPT model for cheaper chat and non-chat tasks GPT-4 Deprecated An older high-intelligence GPT model GPT-4 Turbo Preview Deprecated An older fast GPT model GPT-5.1 Chat Deprecated GPT-5.1 model used in ChatGPT GPT-5 Chat Deprecated GPT-5 model used in ChatGPT text-moderation Deprecated Previous generation text-only moderation model text-moderation-stable Deprecated Previous generation text-only moderation model\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCodex Meetups in Singapore | OpenAI Developers (https://developers.openai.com/community/meetups?city=Singapore)\nciteturn1search10 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; # Codex Meetups\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCodex use cases (https://developers.openai.com/codex/use-cases?category=automation&category=integrations&category=ios&category=knowledge-work&category=quality&task_type=analysis&team=engineering&team=finance&team=quality-engineering&team=research&team=sales)\nciteturn1search11 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 months ago; [Input][Input][Input][Input][Input][Input][Input][Input][Input][Input][Input] [Input: Search Codex use cases]\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"2718d0\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000003333,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":1659,\"output\":\"/Users/julian/.zprofile:source:8: no such file or directory: /Users/julian/.bashrc\\nentire session — Manage agent sessions tracked by Entire\\nView and manage agent sessions tracked by Entire.\\n\\nCommands:\\n  list     List all sessions across all worktrees\\n  info     Show detailed information for a specific session\\n  tokens   Show token usage and optimization recommendations\\n  stop     Stop one or more active sessions\\n  current  Show the active session for the current worktree\\n  attach   Attach an existing agent session\\n  adopt    Adopt an active session from another worktree\\n  resume   Switch to a branch and resume its session\\n\\nExamples:\\n  entire session list                      List all sessions\\n  entire session info <session-id>         Show session details\\n  entire session info <session-id> --json  Output as JSON\\n  entire session tokens <session-id>       Show token usage\\n  entire session stop                      Interactive stop\\n  entire session current                   Active session for cwd\\n  entire session attach <session-id>       Attach an external session\\n  entire session adopt <session-id> --from ../repo  Adopt a moved session\\n  entire session resume <branch>           Resume from a branch\\n\\nCurrent repo: gh/jurei733/testcenter-rewrite  (auto-detected from origin; pass --repo only for a DIFFERENT repo)\\n\\nInherited flags:\\n      --context name   Act as this saved login name for this command only, instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\\n\\nSubcommands: adopt · attach · current · info · list · resume · stop · tokens\\n             read-only except: adopt, attach, resume, stop\\nNext:  entire agent-help session <subcommand>\\nentire doctor — Diagnose and fix session issues\\nScan for session issues and offer to fix them.\\n\\nChecks performed:\\n  1. Disconnected metadata branches: detects when local and remote\\n     entire/checkpoints/v1 branches share no common ancestor (caused by a\\n     previous bug). Fixes by cherry-picking local checkpoints onto remote tip.\\n\\n  2. Operational logs: warn when .entire/logs cannot be written. Every other\\n     diagnostic is delivered by writing there, and that write is silent about\\n     its own failure, so an unwritable log directory looks exactly like a repo\\n     where nothing ran.\\n\\n  When Codex hooks are installed:\\n  3. Codex hook trust: warn when hooks declared in .codex/hooks.json\\n     lack a trusted_hash entry in the user's Codex config (i.e. /hooks\\n     review hasn't run yet on this machine, or a newer entire release\\n     added a hook the user hasn't approved yet).\\n\\n  For each installed agent that reports hook-config drift:\\n  4. Hook config: warn when the installed hooks no longer match what this\\n     CLI writes (e.g. an older release wrote Claude Code tool matchers that\\n     no longer fire, or a committed Pi/OpenCode extension has gone stale).\\n     Fix by re-running 'entire enable --force'.\\n\\n  5. Stuck sessions: sessions stuck in ACTIVE or ENDED phase that need cleanup.\\n\\nA session is considered stuck if:\\n  - It is in ACTIVE phase with no interaction for over 1 hour\\n  - It is in ENDED phase with uncondensed checkpoint data on a shadow branch\\n\\nFor each stuck session, you can choose to:\\n  - Condense: Save session data to permanent storage\\n  - Discard: Remove the session state and shadow branch data\\n  - Skip: Leave the session as-is\\n\\nUse --force to condense all fixable sessions without prompting.  Sessions that can't\\nbe condensed will be discarded.\\n\\nWithout a terminal to prompt on (agents, CI), doctor reports each issue and\\npoints at --force instead of prompting.\\n\\nCurrent repo: gh/jurei733/testcenter-rewrite  (auto-detected from origin; pass --repo only for a DIFFERENT repo)\\n\\nFlags:\\n  -f, --force   Auto-fix all issues without prompting\\n\\nInherited flags:\\n      --context name   Act as this saved login name for this command only, instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\\n\\nSubcommands: bundle · logs · migrate-checkpoints · trace\\n             task-driven\\nNext:  entire agent-help doctor <subcommand>\\ntotal 160\\n-rwxr-xr-x@ 1 julian  staff   478 Apr 25 12:52 applypatch-msg.sample\\n-rwxr-xr-x@ 1 julian  staff   474 Aug 29 21:23 commit-msg\\n-rwxr-xr-x@ 1 julian  staff   896 Apr 25 12:52 commit-msg.sample\\n-rwxr-xr-x@ 1 julian  staff  4726 Apr 25 12:52 fsmonitor-watchman.sample\\n-rwxr-xr-x@ 1 julian  staff   273 Aug 29 21:23 post-commit\\n-rwxr-xr-x@ 1 julian  staff   268 Aug 29 21:23 post-rewrite\\n-rwxr-xr-x@ 1 julian  staff   189 Apr 25 12:52 post-update.sample\\n-rwxr-xr-x@ 1 julian  staff   424 Apr 25 12:52 pre-applypatch.sample\\n-rwxr-xr-x@ 1 julian  staff  1643 Apr 25 12:52 pre-commit.sample\\n-rwxr-xr-x@ 1 julian  staff   416 Apr 25 12:52 pre-merge-commit.sample\\n-rwxr-xr-x@ 1 julian  staff   271 Aug 29 21:23 pre-push\\n-rwxr-xr-x@ 1 julian  staff  1374 Apr 25 12:52 pre-push.sample\\n-rwxr-xr-x@ 1 julian  staff  4898 Apr 25 12:52 pre-rebase.sample\\n-rwxr-xr-x@ 1 julian  staff   544 Apr 25 12:52 pre-receive.sample\\n-rwxr-xr-x@ 1 julian  staff   208 Aug 29 21:23 prepare-commit-msg\\n-rwxr-xr-x@ 1 julian  staff  1492 Apr 25 12:52 prepare-commit-msg.sample\\n-rwxr-xr-x@ 1 julian  staff  2783 Apr 25 12:52 push-to-checkout.sample\\n-rwxr-xr-x@ 1 julian  staff  3650 Apr 25 12:52 update.sample\\n{\\n  \\\"enabled\\\": true,\\n  \\\"absolute_git_hook_path\\\": true,\\n  \\\"checkpoints\\\": {\\n    \\\"primary\\\": {\\n      \\\"type\\\": \\\"git-refs\\\"\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n1010:[hooks.state]\\n1012:[hooks.state.\\\"/Users/julian/Documents/Codex/2026-07-14/echter-lottie-grafikeditor-also-animationen-selbst/.codex/hooks.json:post_tool_use:0:0\\\"]\\n1015:[hooks.state.\\\"/Users/julian/Documents/Codex/2026-07-14/echter-lottie-grafikeditor-also-animationen-selbst/.codex/hooks.json:session_start:0:0\\\"]\\n1018:[hooks.state.\\\"/Users/julian/Documents/Codex/2026-07-14/echter-lottie-grafikeditor-also-animationen-selbst/.codex/hooks.json:user_prompt_submit:0:0\\\"]\\n1021:[hooks.state.\\\"/Users/julian/Documents/Codex/2026-07-14/echter-lottie-grafikeditor-also-animationen-selbst/.codex/hooks.json:stop:0:0\\\"]\\n1024:[hooks.state.\\\"/Users/julian/code/testcenter-rewrite/.codex/hooks.json:post_tool_use:0:0\\\"]\\n1027:[hooks.state.\\\"/Users/julian/code/testcenter-rewrite/.codex/hooks.json:session_start:0:0\\\"]\\n1030:[hooks.state.\\\"/Users/julian/code/testcenter-rewrite/.codex/hooks.json:session_end:0:0\\\"]\\n1033:[hooks.state.\\\"/Users/julian/code/testcenter-rewrite/.codex/hooks.json:user_prompt_submit:0:0\\\"]\\n1036:[hooks.state.\\\"/Users/julian/code/testcenter-rewrite/.codex/hooks.json:subagent_start:0:0\\\"]\\n1039:[hooks.state.\\\"/Users/julian/code/testcenter-rewrite/.codex/hooks.json:subagent_stop:0:0\\\"]\\n1042:[hooks.state.\\\"/Users/julian/code/testcenter-rewrite/.codex/hooks.json:stop:0:0\\\"]\\n\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a07edd-0865-7870-abf3-ba67d94695c7","create_time":1788834829.929964}}}
