{"timestamp":"2026-09-08T02:36:40.918Z","ordinal":60776,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a07edf-f256-7ff3-bdf3-7b9a6e1734b5","call_id":"call_mFx1cSLOl36n6TREpFd3bHBp","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.1 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"a83f96\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000003542,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":1453,\"output\":\"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 1453)\\nTotal output lines: 101\\n\\n/Users/julian/.zprofile:source:8: no such file or directory: /Users/julian/.bashrc\\nExplain provides human-readable context about sessions, commits, and checkpoints.\\n\\nUse this command to understand what happened during agent-driven development,\\neither for self-review or to understand a teammate's work.\\n\\nBy default, shows checkpoints on the current branch. Pass a checkpoint ID or\\ncommit SHA as a positional argument to explain a specific item, or use flags.\\n\\nViewing specific items:\\n  entire checkpoint explain <id-or-sha>           Auto-detects checkpoint ID or commit SHA\\n  entire checkpoint explain --checkpoint <id>     Force interpretation as checkpoint ID\\n  entire checkpoint explain --commit <ref>        Force interpretation as commit ref\\n\\nCheckpoints in another repo:\\n  entire checkpoint explain <id> --repo owner/name\\n                 Explain a checkpoint owned by another repository — the\\n                 drill-down for a cross-repo 'entire search' hit. Reads it from\\n                 that repo's Entire API; nothing is written to this repo.\\n                 Needs a full checkpoint ID (positional or --checkpoint) and a\\n                 checkpoint that has been pushed.\\n\\nFiltering the list view:\\n  --session      Filter checkpoints by session ID (or prefix)\\n\\nOutput verbosity levels (when explaining a specific item):\\n  Default:         Detailed view with scoped prompts (ID, session, tokens, intent, prompts, files)\\n  --short          Summary only (ID, session, timestamp, tokens, intent)\\n  --full           Parsed full transcript (all prompts/responses from entire session)\\n  --raw-transcript Raw transcript file (JSONL format)\\n\\nMachine-readable export modes (additive surface for external consumers):\\n  --json           Metadata-only JSON. Lists checkpoints when no target is given…553 tokens truncated… --json.\\n      --no-pager                      Disable pager output\\n      --raw-transcript                Show raw transcript file (JSONL format)\\n      --repo string                   Explain a checkpoint owned by another repo (owner/name or gh/owner/name), read from that repo's Entire API\\n      --search-all                    Search all commits (no branch/depth limit, may be slow)\\n      --session string                Filter checkpoints by session ID (or prefix)\\n      --session-index int             Session index within a multi-session checkpoint (0-based, defaults to latest) (default -1)\\n  -s, --short                         Show summary only (omit prompts and files)\\n      --summary-timeout-seconds int   Hard deadline in seconds for --generate summary generation; overrides summary_timeout_seconds setting. 0 = use setting; if setting is also unset or 0, no automatic deadline applies.\\n      --transcript                    Stream stored checkpoint transcript bytes to stdout\\n\\nGlobal Flags:\\n      --context name   Act as this saved login name for this command only, instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\\n6640def118bf65e0feff22db46bd43285d8a4f66\\nPreserve participant responses when returning from test completion\\n\\nEntire-Checkpoint: 01M1ZDYH4E0VXGKG2J0SQV6MC3\\n\\ntree c95121733292e0d0cb64f6b64abb8e57cafe4f83\\nauthor jurei733 <67505990+jurei733@users.noreply.github.com> 1788834989 +0200\\ncommitter jurei733 <67505990+jurei733@users.noreply.github.com> 1788834989 +0200\\n\\nCheckpoint: 01M1ZDYH4E0VXGKG2