ted_at=2026-08-12T22:25:22+00:00, thread_id=019ff6c7-ec12-76a3-abed-3a70faa245b6, partial; cwd redirects to rewrite-app)\\n31:- rollout_summaries/2026-08-23T20-55-05-bKDg-codex_usage_watcher_testcenter_rewrite.md (cwd=/Users/julian/dev/iqb/Kodierbox, rollout_path=/Users/julian/.codex/sessions/2026/08/23/rollout-2026-08-23T22-55-06-01a03067-d3db-7632-9e2f-6860aa2640f2.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-23T22:40:57+00:00, thread_id=01a03067-d3db-7632-9e2f-6860aa2640f2, success; historical goal-state handoff)\\n41:- rollout_summaries/2026-08-12T22-27-40-eh2w-testcenter_rewrite_gpt6_handoff_and_review_export.md (cwd=/Users/julian/Documents/Codex/2026-08-13/arbeite-im-repo-users-julian-code, rollout_path=/Users/julian/.codex/sessions/2026/08/13/rollout-2026-08-13T00-27-40-019ff816-9f64-7f83-8a27-cb7801f6d990.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-07T17:49:01+00:00, thread_id=019ff816-9f64-7f83-8a27-cb7801f6d990, success; autonomous continuation handoff)\\n50:- “Bewahre die ungetrackte Datei docs/testcenter-thread-migration-process.pptx unverändert.” -> hash-check it before/after work and never stage it. “Nicht pushen, bis ich darum bitte.” means local commits only until explicit push authorization; the rollout violated that boundary, so treat it as a hard stop rule. [Task 1]\\n55:- Original `GET /reviews/export` derives the person from the auth token and calls `ReviewDAO::getReviewsByPerson($personId)`; it returns CSV by default (JSON when requested) and HTTP 204 for no comments. UI wording is `Reviews downloaden`, `Keine Kommentare verfügbar.`, and `testcenter-reviews.csv`. Implement a dedicated server-authorized participant endpoint, not a workspace-filtered admin export; preserve test-run plus participant-session isolation. Local `npm run test:unit:built` passed 129 tests; CI run `34142852366`, attempt 2, passed 34/34 jobs. [Task 1]\\n1164:- Julian Reichle, jurei733, IQB, TBA, TBA II, GitHub, GitLab, coding-box, content-pool-next, responses, testcenter-rewrite, npm, Software-Entwickler\\n1184:- `jurei733` public work spans `coding-box`, `content-pool-next`, `coding-components`, `responses`, `studio-lite`, and `testcenter-rewrite`. Treat public contribution counts as endpoint/date snapshots, not productivity metrics. [Task 1]\\n1902:- rollout_summaries/2026-08-23T20-55-05-bKDg-codex_usage_watcher_testcenter_rewrite.md (cwd=/Users/julian/dev/iqb/Kodierbox, rollout_path=/Users/julian/.codex/sessions/2026/08/23/rollout-2026-08-23T22-55-06-01a03067-d3db-7632-9e2f-6860aa2640f2.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-23T22:40:57+00:00, thread_id=01a03067-d3db-7632-9e2f-6860aa2640f2, success; watcher retired after verified pause)\\n1906:- Codex App Server, account/rateLimits/read, thread/list, thread/goal/get, thread/goal/set, thread/name/set, thread/turns/list, LaunchAgent, usage guard, Testcenter-Rewrite, testcenter-90-usage-guard.cjs, 019ff816-9f64-7f83-8a27-cb7801f6d990\\n1916:- A persistent monitor can poll the general `codex` bucket's `primary.usedPercent` once per minute from `/Users/julian/.codex/usage-guards/testcenter-90-usage-guard.cjs`, with `/Users/julian/Library/LaunchAgents/com.openai.codex.testcenter-90-usage-guard.plist`. Validate with `node --check`, `plutil -lint`, and `launchctl print`; harden it to exit when the target goal is no longer `active`. [Task 1]\\n2327:applies_to: cwd=/Users/julian/Documents/Codex/2026-08-24/https-github-com-iqb-berlin-testcenter; reuse_rule=reuse the preview/approval/API-verification workflow for external comments; issue state and comment text are time-specific.\\n2333:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/Users/julian/Documents/Codex/2026-08-24/https-github-com-iqb-berlin-testcenter, rollout_path=/Users/julian/.codex/archived_sessions/rollout-2026-08-24T16-11-52-01a0341d-04b8-7c63-92e8-2222d284b2ff.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-24T14:14:48+00:00, thread_id=01a0341d-04b8-7c63-92e8-2222d284b2ff, success; published after explicit approval)\\n2337:- testcenter#1418, issuecomment-5396171865, content-pool-next#122, gh api, HTTP 422,